[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Scandinavian Defense"]
[Variation "Scandinavian Defense: Valencian Variation, Bishop Squeezed on g6"]
[ECO "B01"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Refutes "1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd8 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. h3 Bh5"]
[Themes "bishop-trap,h-pawn-push"]
[Kind "for-us"]

1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd8 4. d4 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. h3 Bh5 7. g4 Bg6 8. Ne5 c6 { Black ignores the danger. Now h4 and h5 will hit the bishop, which has almost nowhere to go. } 9. h4 { Threatens h5, which attacks the bishop on g6. It cannot take on h5 and f5 is covered by the g4 pawn. [%cal Gh4h5] } 9... Be4 { The only way out is to trade itself for the c3 knight on e4. White then has the bishop pair, more space and the better pawns. } *
